.sxng/
tasks/

# Each task gets its own `git worktree add .worktrees/<slug>`; the trees are
# working state, never committed. A given clone may also carry this line in
# `.git/info/exclude`, which does not travel with the repository — this one does.
.worktrees/

# CodeBuddy CLI local artifacts (plugin install cache / staged copies)
.plugins-cache.json
plugins/

# `sessions.md` is a clone-local resume index and `personal.md` is a personal
# rule; neither is ever committed. `hooks/install-git-hygiene` writes both into
# each clone's own `.git/info/exclude`, which is what covers a user's project —
# this file cannot, it only reaches clones of this repository. The line below is
# the other half: a clone of *this* repository that has not run the hooks yet is
# still covered, and the two rules are equivalent, so the union changes nothing.
TaskFlowDocs/**/sessions.md
# Personal rules are local-only and are never committed: everything beside
# TaskFlowDocs/repository-docs/index.md is personal, so ignore its contents
# and re-include the routing record itself.
TaskFlowDocs/repository-docs/*
!TaskFlowDocs/repository-docs/index.md
